{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>Before the year of famine came.</b> Rashi explained that it is forbidden to engage in marital relations in a year of famine. And if you ask: but Levi engaged in marital relations in a year of famine, as our Rabbis said that this was Yocheved, who was born between the walls — one may answer that Joseph had to abstain from marital relations because his father and brothers were in distress, but Levi, who knew that his father lacked nothing, did not have to abstain. And if on Joseph's account — they did not forbid the matter on account of an individual."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:18.257341473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}